Section 2: Technical Approach: The Tolm Substrate
2.1 The Core Innovation Paradigm
The Tolm-Chrono-Dynamic Substrate (Tolm-CDS) completely eliminates the vulnerabilities of conventional
silicon microelectronics (such as copper trace degradation, parasitic capacitance, and radiation-induced latch-up) by
executing computation directly within a software-defined, polarized quantum-vacuum metamaterial.
Auxiliary boundary laser grids drive the interaction zone toward the non-linear Euler-Heisenberg threshold,
altering the spatial refractive index tensor (n) via virtual electron-positron loop excitations. Information processing is
achieved by manipulating the local metric tensor components (gμν) to form discrete, topologically insulated Tolm Cells
(&boldsymbol;ΛTolm(k)).

