Let d denote the exterior derivative and \star the Hodge star operator acting on the 1D spatial Riemannian manifold with metric g = dr \otimes dr.
For a 0-form scalar wavefunction \psi(r):
d\psi = \frac{\partial \psi}{\partial r} dr \star d\psi = \star \left( \frac{\partial \psi}{\partial r} dr \right) = \frac{\partial \psi}{\partial r}
