SECTION 4.1: CUDA C++ ACCELERATOR CORE IMPLEMENTATION
This section contains the production-grade, parallelized CUDA C++ implementation of the Newton-Schulz Matrix Square Root Sandwich Engine (H_{\text{lens}} = K^{1/2} H K^{1/2}).
The code is structured for real-time execution on NVIDIA Tensor Core architectures, using shared memory tiling to achieve sub-millisecond latency for spatial grid sizes N = 240.
